## Nanotechnology
Inkjet Printing and Instant Chemical Transformation of a $\mathsf{C H}_{3}\mathsf{N H}_{3}\mathsf{P b l}_{3}/$ Nanocarbon Electrode and Interface for Planar Perovskite Solar Cells
Inkjet-printing solar cells: By designing carbon plus ${\mathsf{C H}}_{3}{\mathsf{N H}}_{3}|$ ink to transform $\mathsf{P b l}_{2}$ in situ to ${\mathsf{C H}}_{3}{\mathsf{N H}}_{3}{\mathsf{P b l}}_{3}$ , an interpenetrating seamless interface between the ${\mathsf{C H}}_{3}{\mathsf{N H}}_{3}{\mathsf{P b l}}_{3}$ active layer and the C hole-extraction electrode was instantly constructed, resulting in a $11.60\%$ efficient, planar perovskite solar cell.
